{title: Let me walk with you Jesus}
{x_theme: heaven}
{x_source: docx:1. Incomplete/Let me walk with you Jesus.docx}

{comment: Chorus}
Let me walk with you Jesus.
Don’t ever leave me alone.
For without you I could never,
No never make Heaven my home.

{comment: Verse 1}
Now I ‘ve been on the mountain with Jesus.
I’ve been in the valley so low.
But never one time has He failed me,
When to Him with my troubles I go.

{comment: Verse 2}
You found me when I was in trouble.
You found me when I was so blue.
You found me when no one could help me,
And I did not know just what to do.

{comment: Verse 3}
If I had all the wealth of this old world.
If I had all that money could buy.
And I had not the love of my Savior,
Then I would not be ready to die.
